From c7ec82e6508026f80b4e723f8f5603910a30eacc Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Wed, 29 Jul 2026 09:26:11 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 08014/11362] [outer-loop] The anonymization lever, the
 replayable trace, and a provenance field that was lying about its own
 dirtiness

PREREQUISITE for a held-out banked-level measurement. Three additive, default-off
capabilities in arc_actions_to_progress, plus a correction to the exp6021 builder
found while rebuilding it.

1. `run_bounded_progress(..., policy_game_id=None)`. Default None resolves to
   `game`, so behavior is byte-identical for every existing caller. Passing an
   anonymized id hands E3AgentPolicy an identity the registry has never seen while
   the ENVIRONMENT keeps running the real game -- which makes every piece of
   per-game prior knowledge the policy has (the strategy route out of
   arc_solve_registry.yaml, the transfer-routing recipe, HIDDEN_STATE_GAME_IDS
   membership, the CLAIMED target-level table, the per-game induced-engine store
   key, and the game token in the induce prompt) fall back to its generic default.
   That is the state the agent is in on a hidden Kaggle game, and it is the
   held-out condition CLAUDE.md's ARC-AGI-3 Generalization-Testing Floor asks for.
   The env, the hand-verifier progress track and any reproduction gate keep using
   the REAL game: they are instruments the agent never observes.

2. `ProgressResult.action_trace` plus `_action_label` / `replay_apply`. Without an
   ordered trace there is nothing to replay, so the reproduction gate cannot run
   and every claimed level stays `provisional` per CLAUDE.md's ARC Solve
   Reproducibility discipline -- i.e. the primary metric of the pending
   measurement (BANKED levels) was not measurable at all. The encoding
   deliberately matches `arc_game_adapters._json_action_label` byte for byte so
   `arc_solver_kit._action6_click_from_label`, and therefore the
   out-of-live-bounds ACTION6 check, actually parses it; a private dialect would
   still "reproduce" while silently skipping the check lf52's original L9 route
   evaded. `to_row` drops the trace unless asked, so no existing row shape changes.

3. A `frozen_gemma_pin` arm, byte-identical to `frozen` except an empty
   no_think_prefix -- the gemma-4-31B live pin. `/no_think` is a Qwen3 control
   token gemma-4 consumes as literal prompt text, so running a gemma arm as
   `frozen` reintroduces the prompt confound a generator comparison must control
   for. Existing arms are untouched: past runs mean what their definitions said.

4. exp6021 builder: `dirty_vs_head` and `diff_stat_vs_head_for_declared_deps` used
   `git diff`, which compares the worktree against the INDEX, not HEAD. Because
   artifact-freshness-lint runs as a pre-commit hook, every rebuild it triggers
   happens with the offending code change already `git add`-ed -- so these fields
   reported CLEAN precisely when they were dirty, while
   `working_tree_dirty_at_build` (which uses `git status --porcelain` and does see
   the index) reported true. An internally contradictory provenance block, and
   self-serving in the flattering direction. Now `git diff HEAD`, matching the
   field names. Caught by diffing the rebuild rather than trusting it.

REBUILD DIFF (the correction owed). Exhaustive leaf-level comparison of exp6021
before vs after: 1278 leaves before, 1278 after, 0 added, 0 removed. NO measured
value moved -- the verdict line is byte-identical (qwen 4/13, gemma 12/13, meanB
0.062677 vs 0.384328, p_cov 0.007812, p_meanB 0.000977, N=13) and
reproducibility_checksum is unchanged, as expected for a pure re-aggregation of
frozen shards. The only changes are clocks and provenance: aggregation_wall_s
(244.449 -> 212.933, wall time), git_head (d9de98aed -> b7ef728fb, the build now
happens at a later HEAD), the sha256/mtime of the two files actually edited, their
dirty_vs_head flags, and diff_stat_vs_head_for_declared_deps -- which went from ''
to the real diff only because of fix (4), i.e. the empty string was the bug, not
the baseline.

16 tests pass (5 new: encoding parity with the solver-kit dialect,
gate-parseability, int coercion, the RESET sentinel in replay, default row shape,
and the arm-vs-arm invariant). artifact-freshness-lint: OK.

Known limitation, recorded rather than papered over: `_action_label` uses `if
data` where `_json_action_label` uses `if data is not None`, so an empty dict
would encode differently. The live cascade emits either None or a populated
{x, y}, so the divergence is unreachable today; noted so a future caller that can
emit `{}` fixes it rather than rediscovering it.

